<%# Bank node -> config dialog (M2 PR#2b, round 20 progressive rework).
    Default-open state shows the LEAST: the account identity (top-left
    avatar with logo picker, title, subtitle), "Pull From Incomes" and the
    kebab. Everything else is progressive:
      - Pull From Incomes row: checkbox + income name only; the mode select
        and its numeric value are hidden until the row is checked
        (round 20a). Each checkbox is preceded by a hidden enabled=""
        sentinel so an UNCHECK submit reaches the server and removes the
        link (the unchecked-checkbox-sends-nothing Rails gotcha that made
        unchecking "not save").
      - Ownership + role (round 28, R28-4: the round-20f "Details"
        disclosure is gone — always exposed in a bg-surface-inset
        panel). Role offers exactly Savings / Checking / Credit Card /
        Loan / Investment (round 20c); a plain account shows a disabled
        "Plain" placeholder so the browser never silently selects a real
        role.
      - Kebab (round 20b/e): "Make a Sub-Account" popup (select over the
        same candidate set as the old inline select; a "Not a sub-account"
        entry clears it) and "Configure Auto-Transfer" popup (the same
        checkbox list as the old inline section). Both popups live in the
        header, OUTSIDE the form: they sync their state into the form's
        hidden inputs (account[parent_account_id], the "0" sentinel +
        target-id hidden inputs) and their Save buttons submit the form via
        the HTML form= attribute. Data shapes are unchanged
        (parent_account_id, auto_transfer_target_ids fan-out with the "0"
        sentinel stripped server-side).
      - Bank logo (round 20d): the old search + list section is gone. The
        top-left avatar shows the custom upload or the built-in pick
        (neutral circle when empty); clicking it opens a popup with
        "Upload Custom" (POST flow_bank_logo) and a scrollable built-in
        list (data-driven from the available_bank_logos local; the built-in
        set is swapped for favicons in a later round, so nothing hard-
        codes names).
    Submits the PATCH flow_account endpoint: checked rows upsert the edge
    per income, unchecked rows (enabled="") remove the link. In-place
    submit: the diagram tweens to the new graph instead of reloading.
    locals: (account, edges, available_bank_logos: {}) —
    edges: income_series_id -> IncomeAccountAllocation;
    available_bank_logos: slug -> label (BankLogoSlugs.available). %>
<%
  # Round 11 issue 8: fan-out candidate set = the bank rows the planner
  # renders (graph[:banks]) = in-plan accounts + accounts that ARE
  # sub-accounts (parent_account_id set), which the planner includes even
  # without a plan_order (sub_account_links). The auto-transfer popup rows
  # below iterate this set, so a target the diagram draws is always
  # addressable in the dialog. The name-collision guard counts over the
  # same set: when a name occurs 2+ times in it (the dev data has two
  # "SoFi Savings" + two "SoFi Checking"), the row labels for that name get
  # "(<id first 4>)" appended. Label-only.
  in_plan_ids = @in_plan_accounts.map(&:id)
  fanout_rows = @in_plan_accounts.to_a + @flow_accounts.select { |other| other.parent_account_id.present? && !in_plan_ids.include?(other.id) }
  sub_account_name_counts = fanout_rows.group_by(&:name).transform_values(&:size)
  disambiguated_name = lambda do |candidate|
    sub_account_name_counts[candidate.name].to_i > 1 ? "#{candidate.name} (#{candidate.id[0, 4]})" : candidate.name
  end
  # Round 20b: sub-account popup candidate set = the old inline select's
  # options (in-plan accounts that are not themselves sub-accounts).
  sub_account_options = [[ t(".sub_account_none"), "" ]] +
    @in_plan_accounts.reject { |other| other.id == account.id || other.parent_account_id.present? }
                       .map { |other| [ disambiguated_name.call(other), other.id ] }
  # Round 20d: the avatar + logo popup are data-driven off these values.
  avatar_url = account.plan_flow_avatar_url
  logo_custom_url = account.logo.attached? ? Rails.application.routes.url_helpers.rails_blob_path(account.logo, only_path: true) : ""
  logo_list = (available_bank_logos || {}).sort_by { |_slug, label| label.to_s.downcase }.map { |slug, label| { slug: slug, label: label, url: asset_path("bank-logos/#{slug}.svg") } }
  role_options = %w[savings_bucket checking credit_card_payoff loan_payoff investment].map { |role| [ t(".role_#{role}"), role ] }
  # Round 25 (Item 2): the account's target allocation ("Make Allocated
  # Sub-Account"), if any — the kebab swaps the forward action for the
  # REVERSE (the sibling destroy form below) when one exists. Deterministic
  # first row when 2+ exist (same order as the planner's rows).
  target_allocation = Current.family.plan_allocations
    .where(target_account_id: account.id).order(:sort_index, :name, :id).first
  # The allocated-sub popup's default bank source: the opened account's
  # parent pre-checked if it has one, else the first bank row (nil -> the
  # partial's "No bank (unassigned)" row). The user can change it.
  allocated_source_default = account.parent_account_id.presence || @in_plan_accounts.first&.id
  # Round 26 R2 (owner item 3): the "Parent Account" labeled row — the MAIN
  # section (not the kebab), rendered only when the account has a parent
  # link. The display name reuses the fan-out set's name-collision
  # disambiguation (two "SoFi Savings" -> "(6deb)"). The picker's
  # candidate set is the family's TOP-LEVEL accounts (parent_account_id
  # NULL), excluding self; the current parent always satisfies both rules
  # (the validate_parent_change 422 contract), so it is always one of the
  # options.
  parent_account = account.parent_account_id.present? ?
    Current.family.accounts.find_by(id: account.parent_account_id) : nil
  parent_picker_options = parent_account ?
    @flow_accounts.reject { |other| other.id == account.id || other.parent_account_id.present? }
                  .map { |other| [ disambiguated_name.call(other), other.id ] } : []
  # A plain account (nil role) gets a DISABLED placeholder as its selected
  # option: the browser shows it but the user cannot pick it, and the form
  # submits "" which the controller normalizes back to nil. Without this,
  # the first selectable option would render as "selected" and silently
  # promote a plain bank to Savings on the next save.
  role_options.unshift([ t(".role_plain"), "", { disabled: true } ]) if account.plan_role.blank?
%>
<%= render DS::Dialog.new(auto_open: false, disable_frame: true, width: "lg",
      data: {
        node_id: "bank:#{account.id}",
        controller: "bank-config-dialog",
        bank_config_dialog_logos_value: logo_list.to_json,
        # Round 27 (items 3+4): the read-only per-income amounts (series.id
        # => { paycheck: "2700.00", occurrences: 2 }) the Pull-From-Incomes
        # controller's client-side auto-fill / ratio math needs (design
        # R27-T3 §7). JSON (the Stimulus Object value parses it).
        bank_config_dialog_income_amounts_value: (income_amounts || {}).to_json,
        bank_config_dialog_slug_value: account.bank_logo_slug.to_s,
        bank_config_dialog_custom_url_value: logo_custom_url,
        bank_config_dialog_avatar_url_value: avatar_url.to_s,
        bank_config_dialog_upload_url_value: flow_bank_logo_plan_path(account.id),
        bank_config_dialog_remove_url_value: flow_bank_logo_remove_plan_path(account.id)
      }) do |dialog| %>
  <% dialog.with_header(custom_header: true) do %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <%# Round 20d: the account avatar, top-left. Shows the custom upload
          or the built-in pick; neutral circle when empty. Hover reveals
          the pencil; click opens the logo popup (upload + built-ins). %>
      <div class="relative shrink-0" data-bank-config-dialog-target="avatarWrap">
        <button type="button"
                data-bank-config-dialog-target="avatar"
                data-action="bank-config-dialog#openLogo"
                class="group relative h-10 w-10 rounded-full overflow-hidden bg-subdued focus-ring"
                aria-label="<%= t(".logo_popup_title") %>"
                title="<%= t(".logo_hint") %>">
          <%# Both are always rendered (toggled with the hidden class) so
              the Stimulus controller can swap them after an upload /
              removal / pick without rebuilding the node. %>
          <img src="<%= avatar_url %>" alt=""
               class="h-full w-full object-cover <%= "hidden" if avatar_url.blank? %>"
               data-bank-config-dialog-target="avatarImg">
          <span class="flex h-full w-full items-center justify-center text-secondary <%= avatar_url.present? ? "hidden" : "" %>"
                data-bank-config-dialog-target="neutral">
            <%= icon("landmark", size: "sm", color: :secondary) %>
          </span>
          <span class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center bg-inverse/40 opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 group-focus-visible:opacity-100"
                data-bank-config-dialog-target="avatarPencil">
            <%= icon("pencil", size: "xs", color: :white) %>
          </span>
        </button>
        <%# Logo popup: anchored under the avatar. "Upload Custom" (the
            custom logo wins in the avatar when attached), "Remove custom"
            (only when attached), then the scrollable built-in list —
            data-driven (the built-in set is swapped for favicons later). %>
        <div class="hidden absolute left-0 top-full z-30 mt-2 w-72 max-w-[calc(100vw-3rem)] rounded-lg bg-container shadow-border-lg"
             data-bank-config-dialog-target="logoPopup">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-subdued px-3 py-2">
            <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".logo_popup_title") %></p>
            <button type="button" class="text-secondary hover:text-primary"
                    data-action="bank-config-dialog#closePopups"
                    aria-label="<%= t(".logo_popup_title") %>">
              <%= icon("x", size: "xs") %>
            </button>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-2 p-3">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <label class="cursor-pointer rounded-lg border border-primary bg-container px-2 py-1.5 text-xs text-primary hover:bg-subdued/40">
                <%= t(".logo_upload") %>
                <input type="file" accept="image/*" class="sr-only"
                       data-bank-config-dialog-target="fileInput"
                       data-action="bank-config-dialog#uploadLogo">
              </label>
              <button type="button"
                      class="text-xs text-secondary hover:text-destructive underline <%= "hidden" unless account.logo.attached? %>"
                      data-bank-config-dialog-target="removeCustom"
                      data-action="bank-config-dialog#removeCustom">
                <%= t(".logo_remove_custom") %>
              </button>
            </div>
            <p class="hidden text-xs text-destructive" data-bank-config-dialog-target="uploadError"></p>
            <p class="text-xs font-medium text-secondary"><%= t(".logo_builtin_heading") %></p>
            <div class="max-h-48 divide-y divide-subdued overflow-y-auto rounded-lg border border-subdued">
              <button type="button"
                      data-slug=""
                      data-action="bank-config-dialog#pickLogo"
                      class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1.5 text-left hover:bg-subdued/40">
                <span class="flex h-5 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded bg-subdued/60 text-secondary"><%= icon("x", size: "xs") %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-primary truncate"><%= t(".logo_none") %></span>
              </button>
              <% logo_list.each do |entry| %>
                <button type="button"
                        data-slug="<%= entry[:slug] %>"
                        data-action="bank-config-dialog#pickLogo"
                        class="flex w-full items-center gap-2 px-2 py-1.5 text-left hover:bg-subdued/40">
                  <img src="<%= entry[:url] %>" alt="<%= entry[:label] %>"
                       class="h-5 w-8 shrink-0 object-contain">
                  <span class="text-xs text-primary truncate"><%= entry[:label] %></span>
                </button>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <h2 id="<%= dialog.title_id %>" class="font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".title", name: account.name) %></h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-secondary"><%= t(".subtitle") %></p>
      </div>
      <%# Round 20b/e: the kebab. Sub-account + auto-transfer moved out of
          the body into popups; the main form carries the hidden inputs
          they sync into, and the popups' Save buttons submit it via form=. %>
      <div class="relative ml-auto shrink-0" data-bank-config-dialog-target="kebabWrap">
        <button type="button"
                data-bank-config-dialog-target="kebab"
                data-action="bank-config-dialog#toggleKebab"
                class="rounded-lg p-1.5 text-secondary hover:bg-subdued/40 hover:text-primary focus-ring"
                aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-label="<%= t(".more_aria") %>">
          <%= icon("more-vertical", size: "sm") %>
        </button>
        <div class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full z-30 mt-1 w-56 py-1 rounded-lg bg-container shadow-border-lg"
             data-bank-config-dialog-target="kebabMenu">
          <%# Round 26 R2 (owner items 3 + 5): the CONTEXT-AWARE kebab
              matrix.
              Slot 1: a parent link is present -> "Make Parent Account"
              (opens the EXISTING sub-account popup; its "Not a
              sub-account" entry clears the link through the same
              syncSubAccount + validate_parent_change 422 contract);
              else -> "Make a Sub-Account" (unchanged).
              Slot 2: a target allocation is present -> "Make Parent
              Account" (submits the EXISTING reverse form
              allocated_reverse_<id> = DELETE the target allocation; the
              account's row reappears per the draw priority — sub row if
              parent-linked, bank row if plan_order, unplaced otherwise);
              else -> "Make Allocated Sub-Account" (the forward popup).
              Slot 3: "Configure Auto-Transfer" — LAST (owner item 5: not
              in the middle). A dressed+parent account renders BOTH
              "Make Parent Account" items (slot 1 clears the link, slot 2
              destroys the target) — two adjacent items sharing a label
              is the owner-accepted reading (no live instance today).
              Slot 1 is ABSENT for a dressed account without a parent
              (the spec's dressed state = the reverse + auto-transfer,
              2 items — a dressed account offers no forward
              "Make a Sub-Account" while it sits in the allocation
              pillar). %>
          <% unless target_allocation && !account.parent_account_id.present? %>
            <button type="button"
                    class="block w-full px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm text-primary hover:bg-subdued/40"
                    data-action="bank-config-dialog#openSubAccount">
              <%= t(account.parent_account_id.present? ? ".make_parent_account" : ".menu_make_sub_account") %>
            </button>
          <% end %>
          <% if target_allocation %>
            <button type="submit"
                    form="allocated_reverse_<%= account.id %>"
                    class="block w-full px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm text-primary hover:bg-subdued/40">
              <%= t(".make_parent_account") %>
            </button>
          <% else %>
            <button type="button"
                    class="block w-full px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm text-primary hover:bg-subdued/40"
                    data-action="bank-config-dialog#openAllocatedSub">
              <%= t(".menu_make_allocated_sub_account") %>
            </button>
          <% end %>
          <button type="button"
                  class="block w-full px-3 py-2 text-left text-sm text-primary hover:bg-subdued/40"
                  data-action="bank-config-dialog#openAutoTransfer">
            <%= t(".menu_configure_auto_transfer") %>
          </button>
        </div>
        <%# Round 25 (Item 2): the "Make Allocated Sub-Account" popup
            (only for a plain account — a dressed one renders the REVERSE
            instead). Unlike the sibling popups (which sync the main form's
            hidden inputs and submit it via form=), this one is a
            SELF-CONTAINED form: its own fields POST the create-allocation
            endpoint directly (no JS sync, no shared-form crosstalk). The
            document-level in-place submit handler intercepts it like every
            other plan-flow form. The dialog re-renders fully on every
            save, so every default here is server-rendered — no JS state
            survives a round trip (the house contract). The value input is
            renamed by #syncAllocatedMode (plan_allocation[value] vs
            [value_percent], the allocation dialog's own mode sync is
            form-scoped and cannot see this popup). %>
        <% unless target_allocation %>
        <%= form_with url: flow_allocation_create_plan_path, method: :post,
                      scope: :plan_allocation,
                      html: { id: "allocated_sub_form_#{account.id}" },
                      class: "hidden absolute right-0 top-full z-40 mt-1 w-72 space-y-2 rounded-lg bg-container p-3 shadow-border-lg",
                      data: {
                        turbo: "false",
                        plan_flow_inplace: "true",
                        bank_config_dialog_target: "allocatedSubPopup"
                      } do %>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_title") %></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_hint") %></p>
          <%# Name: prefilled with the opened account name, editable. %>
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <label class="block text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_name") %></label>
            <input type="text" name="plan_allocation[name]" value="<%= account.name %>"
                   required class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full">
          </div>
          <%# The same amount control as the allocation dialog (the owner's
              "How much you want to put in there"): mode select + the value
              input it renames. kind is fixed to savings — the "Allocation
              Role" of a dressed account (the planner's money-destination
              autofill kind); the popup offers no kind control. %>
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <label class="block text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_amount") %></label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <select name="plan_allocation[mode]"
                      data-action="bank-config-dialog#syncAllocatedMode"
                      class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-28 shrink-0">
                <% PlanAllocation.modes.each_key do |mode| %>
                  <option value="<%= mode %>" <%= "selected" if mode == "required" %>>
                    <%= t("plan_flows.allocation_dialog.mode_#{mode}") %>
                  </option>
                <% end %>
              </select>
              <input type="text" name="plan_allocation[value]" placeholder="0.00"
                     class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full tabular-nums"
                     data-bank-config-dialog-target="allocatedValue">
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_amount_hint") %></p>
          </div>
          <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[kind]" value="savings">
          <input type="hidden" name="plan_allocation[target_account_id]" value="<%= account.id %>">
          <%# Bank source: the plan's rows — the SAME partial the allocation
              dialog renders (radio name plan_allocation[account_id] stays
              the save contract); the opened account's parent pre-checked
              if it has one, else the first bank row. %>
          <p class="text-xs font-medium text-secondary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_source") %></p>
          <%= render "plan_flows/allocation_bank_rows",
                bank_rows: @in_plan_accounts,
                checked_account_id: allocated_source_default,
                account_last4s: @account_last4s %>
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".allocated_sub_source_hint") %></p>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
            <button type="button"
                    class="rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-primary"
                    data-action="bank-config-dialog#closePopups">
              <%= t(".popup_cancel") %>
            </button>
            <button type="submit"
                    class="rounded-lg bg-primary px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-on-primary hover:opacity-90">
              <%= t(".save") %>
            </button>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <% end %>
        <%# Sub-account popup (round 20b): same candidate set + "Not a
            sub-account" clear as the removed inline select; live-syncs
            account[parent_account_id] in the form. %>
        <div class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full z-40 mt-1 w-72 space-y-2 rounded-lg bg-container p-3 shadow-border-lg"
             data-bank-config-dialog-target="subAccountPopup">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".menu_make_sub_account") %></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".sub_account_hint") %></p>
          <select data-bank-config-dialog-target="subAccountSelect"
                  data-action="bank-config-dialog#syncSubAccount"
                  class="w-full rounded-lg border border-primary bg-container px-2 py-1.5 text-sm text-primary">
            <% sub_account_options.each do |label, value| %>
              <option value="<%= value %>" <%= "selected" if value.to_s == account.parent_account_id.to_s %>><%= label %></option>
            <% end %>
          </select>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
            <button type="button"
                    class="rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-primary"
                    data-action="bank-config-dialog#closePopups">
              <%= t(".popup_cancel") %>
            </button>
            <button type="submit" form="bank_config_form_<%= account.id %>"
                    class="rounded-lg bg-primary px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-on-primary hover:opacity-90">
              <%= t(".save") %>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <%# Auto-transfer popup (round 20e): the same checkbox list the
            old inline section had (disabled unless a sub-account of this
            account); live-rebuilds the form's hidden target-id inputs
            (the "0" sentinel stays, so an all-unchecked save clears). %>
        <div class="hidden absolute right-0 top-full z-40 mt-1 max-h-80 w-72 space-y-2 overflow-y-auto rounded-lg bg-container p-3 shadow-border-lg"
             data-bank-config-dialog-target="autoTransferPopup">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".auto_transfer_targets") %></p>
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".auto_transfer_targets_hint") %></p>
          <div class="space-y-1" data-bank-config-dialog-target="autoTransferBox">
            <% fanout_rows.each do |other| %>
              <% is_sub_account = other.parent_account_id == account.id %>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
                <input type="checkbox"
                       data-other-id="<%= other.id %>"
                       <%= "checked" if Array(account.auto_transfer_target_ids).include?(other.id) %>
                       <%= "disabled" unless is_sub_account %>
                       data-action="bank-config-dialog#syncAutoTransfer"
                       class="checkbox checkbox--light h-4 w-4 rounded shrink-0">
                <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm text-primary" title="<%= disambiguated_name.call(other) %>">
                  <%= disambiguated_name.call(other) %>
                </span>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-end gap-2">
            <button type="button"
                    class="rounded-lg px-2.5 py-1.5 text-sm text-secondary hover:text-primary"
                    data-action="bank-config-dialog#closePopups">
              <%= t(".popup_cancel") %>
            </button>
            <button type="submit" form="bank_config_form_<%= account.id %>"
                    class="rounded-lg bg-primary px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-on-primary hover:opacity-90">
              <%= t(".save") %>
            </button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <%= render DS::Button.new(variant: "icon", size: :sm, icon: "x", type: "button",
                                 title: I18n.t("ds.dialog.close"),
                                 aria: { label: I18n.t("ds.dialog.close") },
                                 data: { action: "DS--dialog#close" }) %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <% dialog.with_body do %>
    <%# In-place validation errors (owner round 3, R1/R7): the 422 response
        renders them here — no full-reload flash for in-place submits. %>
    <div data-in-place-errors class="hidden space-y-1"></div>
    <%# In-place submit (owner round 3, R1/R7): data-turbo off + the
        in-place submit handler — the diagram tweens to the new graph
        instead of a full reload destroying it. The id backs the popup
        Save buttons' form= attribute (the popups live in the header,
        outside this form). %>
    <%= form_with url: flow_account_plan_path(account.id), method: :patch, scope: :account,
                  class: "space-y-5",
                  html: { id: "bank_config_form_#{account.id}" },
                  data: { turbo: "false", plan_flow_inplace: "true" } do |form| %>
      <%# Hidden state the header popups sync (the popups are outside the
          form): the logo slug (the logo popup writes it), the sub-account
          parent (the sub-account popup writes it), and the auto-transfer
          fan-out — the "0" sentinel makes an all-unchecked submit clear
          the array (the server strips it); the checked target ids are the
          data-marked hidden inputs the auto-transfer popup rebuilds in
          row order. %>
      <%# Round 27 (item 7): the active Per Paycheck / Per Month view.
          The view toggle is a full-reload link, so this hidden input is
          always fresh when the in-place submit (fetch + FormData) posts
          it — the re-rendered chrome re-renders the dialogs in the same
          view unit. (The controller's flow_view only reads params[:view]
          on the graph/draft paths; the dialog save path uses it too.) %>
      <input type="hidden" name="view" value="<%= view %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="account[bank_logo_slug]" value="<%= account.bank_logo_slug %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="account[parent_account_id]" value="<%= account.parent_account_id %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="account[auto_transfer_target_ids][]" value="0" class="sr-only">
      <% Array(account.auto_transfer_target_ids).each do |target_id| %>
        <input type="hidden" name="account[auto_transfer_target_ids][]" value="<%= target_id %>"
               data-auto-transfer-tid="1">
      <% end %>

      <%# Round 26 R2 (owner item 3): the "Parent Account" labeled row —
          the MAIN section (not the kebab dropdown), shown only when the
          account has a parent link (sub or dressed+parent). The label
          shows the parent's disambiguated name; the picker (NEW target
          name: mainParentSelect — no collision with the header popups')
          offers the family's top-level accounts (parent NULL) excluding
          self and live-syncs the form's hidden account[parent_account_id]
          — the dialog's Save submits it through the validate_parent_change
          422 contract (the same path as the sub-account popup). %>
      <% if parent_account %>
        <section class="space-y-1" data-bank-config-dialog-target="parentRow">
          <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".parent_account") %></p>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate text-sm text-primary"
                  title="<%= disambiguated_name.call(parent_account) %>">
              <%= disambiguated_name.call(parent_account) %>
            </span>
            <select data-bank-config-dialog-target="mainParentSelect"
                    data-action="change->bank-config-dialog#syncMainParent"
                    aria-label="<%= t(".parent_account") %>"
                    class="w-44 shrink-0 text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary">
              <% parent_picker_options.each do |label, value| %>
                <option value="<%= value %>" <%= "selected" if value == account.parent_account_id %>><%= label %></option>
              <% end %>
            </select>
          </div>
        </section>
      <% end %>

      <%# Round 20a / Round 27 (owner items 3+4): "Pull From Incomes" —
          the default-visible income section. Round 27 restyle: the native
          mode select is an R26-style trigger button + floating option
          panel (reusing the dialog's floatLayer/#floatPopup machinery),
          and the SUBMIT carriers are the per-income hidden inputs
          (links[<id>][mode|value]) — the R26 trigger pattern: the visible
          controls are nameless and the dialog controller live-syncs the
          hidden inputs, which is what save_bank_links sees (the param
          contract is byte-identical). With 2+ incomes checked the per-row
          details collapse into the shared control set after the rows (mode
          trigger, then the Ratio trigger, then the amount input — the
          owner's exact placement). The Ratio is NEVER submitted (design
          R27-T3 §3 decision (a)): it is re-derived below from the stored
          per-income values + the read-only income amounts so a re-open
          shows the same numbers. Round 30: the REQUIRED-mode split
          percents RIDE the existing links[<id>][value] carrier (2 dp
          major units of the bank's required amount; blank = nil = the
          equal split) — the only value save_bank_links sees. The hidden
          enabled="" sentinel before
          each checkbox stays the round-20 save fix: an unchecked Rails
          checkbox sends nothing, so the sentinel is what reaches the
          controller with an empty value and destroys the link; when
          checked, the checkbox's own "1" follows the sentinel and wins. %>
      <%
        checked_series = @income_series.select { |s| edges[s.id] }
        n_checked = checked_series.size
        # income_amounts: series.id => { paycheck: "2700.00",
        # occurrences: 2 } (the read-only dialog context; nil-safe so a
        # partial render without it degrades to the no-amounts math).
        income_pp = (income_amounts || {}).transform_values { |a| a[:paycheck].to_d }
        income_counts = (income_amounts || {}).transform_values { |a| a[:occurrences].to_i }
        pp_sum = checked_series.sum { |s| income_pp.fetch(s.id, BigDecimal(0)) }
        total_events = checked_series.sum { |s| income_counts.fetch(s.id, 0) }
        # Combined paychecks per month (4 events / 2 incomes = 2): the
        # monthly-total -> per-paycheck conversion factor for the shared
        # input (stored values are per-paycheck; the input renders in the
        # active view unit — Q7).
        combined_pp_count = n_checked.positive? ? (total_events / n_checked) : 1
        shared = n_checked >= 2
        shared_modes = checked_series.map { |s| edges[s.id].mode }.uniq
        shared_mixed = shared && shared_modes.size > 1
        shared_mode = shared ? (shared_mixed ? "mixed" : shared_modes.first) : nil
        # Ratio re-derivation from the stored per-income values (specific:
        # equal dollars <= 1c, then dollars proportional to the income
        # amounts <= 1c, else fixed amounts; percent: equal fractions <=
        # 0.01p, then equal dollar contributions <= 1c, else fixed
        # amounts; required — Round 30 D-REOPEN: all-nil or
        # each-within-1c-of-100/n -> equal, each-within-1c of the strict
        # income-proportional percents -> rational, otherwise percent
        # (the typed percents — a saved 75/25 re-opens as Percent)).
        # Leftover carries no ratio (hidden).
        pull_ratio = "hidden"
        if shared && !shared_mixed && %w[specific percent].include?(shared_mode) && n_checked >= 2
          vals = checked_series.map { |s| edges[s.id].value }
          if shared_mode == "specific"
            total = vals.sum
            rational = pp_sum.positive? && vals.each_index.all? do |i|
              (vals[i] - total * income_pp.fetch(checked_series[i].id, BigDecimal(0)) / pp_sum).abs <= 0.01
            end
            pull_ratio = (vals[0] - vals[1]).abs <= 0.01 ? "equal" : (rational ? "rational" : "fixed_amounts")
          else
            dollars = checked_series.each_index.map { |i| vals[i] * income_pp.fetch(checked_series[i].id, BigDecimal(0)) }
            pull_ratio = (vals[0] - vals[1]).abs <= 0.0001 ? "rational" : ((dollars[0] - dollars[1]).abs <= 0.01 ? "equal" : "fixed_amounts")
          end
        elsif shared && !shared_mixed && shared_mode == "required"
          vals = checked_series.map { |s| edges[s.id].value }
          all_equal = vals.each_index.all? do |i|
            vals[i].nil? || (vals[i].to_d - (BigDecimal(100) / n_checked)).abs <= 0.01
          end
          rational = pp_sum.positive? && vals.each_index.all? do |i|
            !vals[i].nil? && (vals[i].to_d - BigDecimal(100) * income_pp.fetch(checked_series[i].id, BigDecimal(0)) / pp_sum).abs <= 0.01
          end
          pull_ratio = vals.all?(&:nil?) || all_equal ? "equal" : (rational ? "rational" : "percent")
        end
        pull_ratio = "fixed_amounts" if shared_mixed
        shared_ratio_shown = shared && (shared_mixed || %w[specific percent required].include?(shared_mode))
        shared_split_hidden = shared && (shared_mixed || pull_ratio == "fixed_amounts")
        # The shared single input's initial text (view unit): specific =
        # the total (per combined paycheck, or monthly when Per Month),
        # percent-rational = the common percent, percent-equal = the total
        # dollars per combined paycheck as a percent of the combined
        # paycheck. Required/leftover carry no stored value (""; the JS
        # fills the locked auto-fill on connect).
        shared_single = ""
        if shared && !shared_mixed && !shared_split_hidden
          if shared_mode == "specific"
            total_pp = checked_series.sum { |s| edges[s.id].value }
            shared_single = format("%.2f", view == "monthly" ? total_pp * combined_pp_count : total_pp)
          elsif shared_mode == "percent"
            if pull_ratio == "rational"
              shared_single = format("%.2f", edges[checked_series[0].id].value * 100)
            else
              total_pp = checked_series.sum { |s| edges[s.id].value }
              shared_single = pp_sum.zero? ? "" : format("%.2f", total_pp / pp_sum * 100)
            end
          end
        end
        # The required display in the active view unit (nil when the bank
        # has no required base: the label hides, the Required input shows
        # "—").
        required_display = required_display_amount && !required_display_amount.zero? ? format("%.2f", required_display_amount) : nil
      %>
      <section class="space-y-2" data-bank-config-dialog-target="pullFrom"
               data-bank-view="<%= view %>"
               data-bank-required-display="<%= required_display %>"
               data-bank-pull-from-ratio="<%= shared ? pull_ratio : "hidden" %>"
               data-bank-required-amount-label="<%= t(".required_amount_label") %>"
               data-bank-required-amount-total-label="<%= t(".required_amount_total_label") %>"
               data-bank-per-income-readout="<%= t(".per_income_readout") %>"
               data-bank-per-income-readout-percent="<%= t(".per_income_readout_percent") %>"
               data-bank-mixed-label="<%= t(".mixed_modes") %>"
               data-bank-required-note="<%= t(".ratio_hidden_hint") %>"
               data-bank-leftover-note="<%= t(".ratio_leftover_hint") %>"
               data-bank-ratio-equal="<%= t(".ratio_equal") %>"
               data-bank-ratio-rational="<%= t(".ratio_rational") %>"
               data-bank-ratio-fixed-amounts="<%= t(".ratio_fixed_amounts") %>"
               data-bank-ratio-percent="<%= t(".ratio_percent") %>"
               data-bank-total-label="<%= t(".total_amount_label") %>"
               data-bank-percent-hint="<%= t(".percent_hint") %>">
        <p class="text-sm font-medium text-primary"><%= t(".pull_from_incomes") %></p>
        <% if @income_series.empty? %>
          <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= t(".no_incomes") %></p>
        <% end %>
        <%# Round 29 (R29-1): each_with_index — the shared control set
            moved OUT of the loop (it now renders below all the rows, after
            the loop's end); the index is no longer referenced inside. %>
        <% @income_series.each_with_index do |series, i| %>
          <% edge = edges[series.id] %>
          <%# State A single value (view unit): required = the required
              display (locked auto-fill), leftover = "", specific = the
              stored per-paycheck amount (monthly view: x its occurrence
              count), percent = the stored fraction x 100 (view-
              independent). %>
          <% row_single = if edge.nil?
                            ""
                          elsif edge.mode == "required"
                            required_display || "—"
                          elsif edge.mode == "leftover"
                            ""
                          else
                            format("%.2f", edge.mode == "specific" ? (view == "monthly" ? edge.value * income_counts.fetch(series.id, 1) : edge.value) : edge.value * 100)
                          end %>
          <%# The greyed per-income readout (State B only; the dialog
              controller fills it). Round 30: server-seeded for the
              required split — 50/50 / Proportional AND Percent (W2: the $
              readouts stay visible next to the % inputs; only Fixed
              Amounts hides them for its $ inputs). The JS re-derives the
              same on connect; hidden otherwise. %>
          <% required_readout = if shared && !shared_mixed && shared_mode == "required" && %w[equal rational percent].include?(pull_ratio)
                                  split = (required_splits || {})[series.id]
                                  split ? t(".per_income_readout", name: series.name, amount: split[:display]) : nil
                                end %>
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap" data-bank-row data-bank-series-id="<%= series.id %>">
            <input type="hidden" name="links[<%= series.id %>][enabled]" value="">
            <input type="checkbox"
                   name="links[<%= series.id %>][enabled]" value="1"
                   <%= "checked" if edge %>
                   class="checkbox checkbox--light h-4 w-4 rounded shrink-0"
                   data-action="change->bank-config-dialog#syncBankRow">
            <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 basis-32 truncate text-sm text-primary" title="<%= series.name %>"
                  data-bank-row-name><%= series.name %></span>
            <span class="<%= required_readout ? "ml-auto " : "hidden ml-auto " %>text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums" data-bank-per-income-readout><%= required_readout %></span>
            <%# Round 28 (R28-3): the Fixed Amounts per-row $ input + the
                mixed-state mode tag live inline at the row's right end
                (moved from the old bottom-center split wrap). The
                server-rendered value seeds the mixed-state pre-fill; the
                dialog controller toggles hidden — the readout and the
                input are mutually exclusive per row. %>
            <input type="text"
                   value="<%= edges[series.id] ? (edges[series.id].mode == "specific" ? format("%.2f", edges[series.id].value) : (edges[series.id].mode == "percent" ? format("%.2f", edges[series.id].value * 100) : (edges[series.id].mode == "required" && pull_ratio == "percent" && edges[series.id].value ? format("%.2f", edges[series.id].value) : ""))) : "" %>"
                   placeholder="0.00"
                   class="<%= shared && !shared_mixed && shared_mode == "required" && pull_ratio == "percent" ? "" : "hidden" %> text-xs border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1 bg-container text-primary w-20 shrink-0 tabular-nums"
                   data-bank-split-input="<%= series.id %>"
                   data-action="input->bank-config-dialog#recalcPullFrom">
            <span class="hidden text-xs text-secondary rounded bg-surface-inset px-1 shrink-0" data-bank-mode-tag="<%= series.id %>"></span>
            <div class="<%= "hidden " unless edge %>flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap" data-bank-row-details>
              <%# The row's submit carriers (R26 trigger pattern): the
                  hidden mode + value inputs are what submits. Mode
                  defaults to "required" for an unchecked row (the
                  sentinel destroys it on save anyway); value mirrors the
                  stored per-paycheck amount (specific, major units) or
                  0-100 (percent). The JS live-syncs them from the
                  visible controls. %>
              <input type="hidden" name="links[<%= series.id %>][mode]" value="<%= edge ? edge.mode : "required" %>">
              <%# Round 30: the required-mode [value] carrier transitions
                  from always-blank to the stored 2-dp percent of the bank's
                  required amount (blank = nil = the equal split). %>
              <input type="hidden" name="links[<%= series.id %>][value]" value="<%= edge ? (edge.mode == "specific" ? format("%.2f", edge.value) : (edge.mode == "percent" ? format("%.2f", edge.value * 100) : (edge.mode == "required" && edge.value ? format("%.2f", edge.value) : ""))) : "" %>">
              <%# Mode trigger (the R26 pattern): the visible control is a
                  button; the panel radios sync the hidden mode input. %>
              <button type="button"
                      data-action="click->bank-config-dialog#openPullPanel"
                      data-bank-pull-panel-group="row-<%= series.id %>"
                      aria-label="<%= t(".rule_aria", name: series.name) %>"
                      class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 min-h-9 rounded-lg px-2 cursor-pointer bg-container border border-primary text-xs text-primary w-44 shrink-0">
                <span class="truncate" data-bank-pull-mode-label><%= edge ? t(".mode_#{edge.mode}") : t(".mode_required") %></span>
                <%= icon "chevron-down", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0 text-secondary" %>
              </button>
              <div class="hidden absolute left-0 top-full z-30 mt-1 w-44 rounded-lg bg-container p-1 shadow-border-lg"
                   data-bank-pull-panel data-bank-pull-panel-group="row-<%= series.id %>">
                <% %w[required specific percent leftover].each do |mode| %>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
                    <input type="radio" name="pull-row-mode-<%= series.id %>" value="<%= mode %>"
                           class="sr-only"
                           <%= "checked" if edge&.mode == mode %>
                           data-action="change->bank-config-dialog#setPullMode">
                    <span class="text-xs text-primary"><%= t(".mode_#{mode}") %></span>
                  </label>
                <% end %>
              </div>
              <%# Greyed "Required Amount: $X" (only Fixed/Percent with X >
                  0; the JS fills + toggles it). %>
              <p class="hidden text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums" data-bank-required-label></p>
              <%# Nameless value input (the hidden links[<id>][value]
                  submits): locked+auto-filled for Required, disabled+
                  empty for Leftover, editable for Fixed/Percent. %>
              <input type="text"
                     value="<%= row_single %>"
                     placeholder="<%= edge&.mode == "percent" ? t(".percent_placeholder") : t(".specific_placeholder") %>"
                     <%= "disabled" unless edge && %w[specific percent].include?(edge.mode) %>
                     class="text-xs border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1 bg-container text-primary w-20 shrink-0 tabular-nums"
                     data-bank-pull-row-value
                     data-action="input->bank-config-dialog#recalcPullFrom">
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
        <%# Round 29 (R29-1): the shared control set renders BELOW all the
            income rows — the owner's placement change (R28-3 had it between
            the rows; below flows better per the owner). Emitted whenever
            2+ income series exist; the dialog controller hides it (hidden
            class on data-bank-pull-from-shared) unless 2+ are checked
            (shared state) — the visibility toggle is unchanged. Contents/
            behavior identical to the R28-3 block: the grey Mode / Split
            Behavior labels above the two triggers, then the control row —
            mode trigger (the shared amount source, sign-off Q1-A), the
            split-icon behavior trigger, the conditional total input (R29-2:
            w-40, the same width as the trigger boxes), the running total
            right-aligned. Section order: rows -> Split Options -> the
            Ownership + Role panel below the section (unchanged). %>
        <% if @income_series.size >= 2 %>
          <div class="pl-6 py-1 <%= "hidden" unless shared %>" data-bank-pull-from-shared>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
              <span class="text-xs text-secondary w-40"><%= t(".mode_label") %></span>
              <span class="text-xs text-secondary w-40"><%= t(".split_behavior_label") %></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap">
              <button type="button"
                      data-action="click->bank-config-dialog#openPullPanel"
                      data-bank-pull-panel-group="shared-mode"
                      class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 min-h-9 rounded-lg px-2 cursor-pointer bg-container border border-primary text-xs w-40 shrink-0">
                <span class="truncate <%= shared_mixed ? "text-secondary" : "text-primary" %>" data-bank-pull-shared-mode-label>
                  <%= shared_mixed ? t(".mixed_modes") : t(".mode_#{shared_mode || 'required'}") %>
                </span>
                <%= icon "chevron-down", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0 text-secondary" %>
              </button>
              <%# Shared-mode panel (R5 fix): the radios sync the hidden
                  links[<id>][mode] inputs of every checked row via
                  setPullMode (group "shared-mode"). None is checked in the
                  mixed stored-modes state — picking one resolves it. %>
              <div class="hidden absolute left-0 top-full z-30 mt-1 w-40 rounded-lg bg-container p-1 shadow-border-lg"
                   data-bank-pull-panel data-bank-pull-panel-group="shared-mode">
                <% %w[required specific percent leftover].each do |mode| %>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
                    <input type="radio" name="pull-shared-mode-<%= account.id %>" value="<%= mode %>"
                           class="sr-only"
                           <%= "checked" if shared_mode == mode %>
                           data-action="change->bank-config-dialog#setPullMode">
                    <span class="text-xs text-primary"><%= t(".mode_#{mode}") %></span>
                  </label>
                <% end %>
              </div>
              <%# Behavior trigger (the split icon): visible for every
                  shared mode per sign-off §8.1 — greyed + non-interactive
                  under Required / Leftover / mixed (the JS toggles the wrap
                  + disabled on connect and on every recalc). %>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap <%= "hidden" unless shared_ratio_shown %>" data-bank-pull-ratio-wrap>
                <button type="button"
                        <%= "disabled" if shared_mixed %>
                        data-action="click->bank-config-dialog#openPullPanel"
                        data-bank-pull-panel-group="shared-ratio"
                        class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 min-h-9 rounded-lg px-2 cursor-pointer bg-container border border-primary text-xs w-40 shrink-0 <%= shared_mixed ? "text-secondary" : "text-primary" %>">
                  <%= icon "split", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0 text-secondary" %>
                  <span class="truncate" data-bank-pull-ratio-label>
                    <% case pull_ratio
                       when "equal" then t(".ratio_equal")
                       when "rational" then t(".ratio_rational")
                       when "fixed_amounts" then t(".ratio_fixed_amounts")
                       when "percent" then t(".ratio_percent")
                       else t(".ratio_rational")
                       end %>
                  </span>
                  <%= icon "chevron-down", size: "sm", class: "shrink-0 text-secondary" %>
                </button>
                <div class="hidden absolute left-0 top-full z-30 mt-1 w-40 rounded-lg bg-container p-1 shadow-border-lg"
                     data-bank-pull-panel data-bank-pull-panel-group="shared-ratio">
                  <% %w[equal rational fixed_amounts].each do |ratio| %>
                    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset">
                      <input type="radio" name="pull-shared-ratio-<%= account.id %>" value="<%= ratio %>"
                             class="sr-only"
                             <%= "checked" if pull_ratio == ratio %>
                             data-action="change->bank-config-dialog#setSharedRatio">
                      <span class="text-xs text-primary"><%= t(".ratio_#{ratio}") %></span>
                    </label>
                  <% end %>
                  <%# Round 30: the 4th behavior option (Percent of the
                      required amount) — a Required-mode-only control: the
                      wrapper renders hidden + the radio disabled unless the
                      stored shared mode is required (the JS recalc mirrors
                      the same live toggle on every mode change). %>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 cursor-pointer has-[:checked]:bg-surface-inset <%= shared_mode == "required" ? "" : "hidden" %>" data-bank-ratio-percent-option>
                    <input type="radio" name="pull-shared-ratio-<%= account.id %>" value="percent"
                           class="sr-only"
                           <%= "checked" if pull_ratio == "percent" %>
                           <%= "disabled" if shared_mode != "required" %>
                           data-action="change->bank-config-dialog#setSharedRatio">
                    <span class="text-xs text-primary"><%= t(".ratio_percent") %></span>
                  </label>
                </div>
              </div>
              <%# The single amount input (view unit): total-$ for Fixed
                  Amount, %-of-combined for Percent, locked auto-filled for
                  Required, locked empty for Leftover. %>
              <div class="flex items-center gap-2 self-center" data-bank-pull-single-wrap>
                <input type="text"
                       value="<%= shared_single %>"
                       placeholder="0.00"
                       class="text-xs border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1 bg-container text-primary w-40 shrink-0 tabular-nums min-h-9"
                       data-bank-pull-shared-value
                       data-action="input->bank-config-dialog#recalcPullFrom">
              </div>
              <p class="ml-auto hidden text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums" data-bank-split-total></p>
            </div>
            <%# Greyed label/note (the JS fills + toggles them): the
                "Required Amount: $X (total)" label (specific, X > 0) /
                plain label (percent) / the required + leftover notes. The
                percent hint follows the single input (its old spot). %>
            <p class="hidden text-xs text-secondary tabular-nums" data-bank-pull-required-label></p>
            <p class="hidden text-xs text-secondary" data-bank-pull-mode-note></p>
            <p class="hidden text-xs text-secondary" data-bank-percent-hint></p>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </section>
    <%# Round 28 (R28-4): the "Details" disclosure is gone — Ownership +
        Role stay always exposed, wrapped in a slightly-darker soft-
        cornered panel (bg-surface-inset rounded-xl p-3) so they read as
        secondary to the Pull From Incomes section. Rendered inside the
        form (plain inputs with explicit name= — the strings are the
        pre-resolved locals). %>
    <% ownership_label_text = t(".ownership_label") %>
    <% role_label_text = t(".role_label") %>
    <% ownership_shared_text = t(".ownership_shared") %>
    <div class="bg-surface-inset rounded-xl p-3">
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <label for="account_plan_ownership_<%= account.id %>" class="block text-xs text-secondary">
            <%= ownership_label_text %>
          </label>
          <select id="account_plan_ownership_<%= account.id %>" name="account[plan_ownership]"
                  class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full">
            <%= options_for_select(
                  [[ ownership_shared_text, "shared" ]] + @family_users.map { |user| [ user.display_name, "user:#{user.id}" ] },
                  account.plan_ownership == "user" ? "user:#{account.plan_owner_user_id}" : "shared"
              ) %>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <label for="account_plan_role_<%= account.id %>" class="block text-xs text-secondary">
            <%= role_label_text %>
          </label>
          <%# Round 20c: exactly Savings / Checking / Credit Card / Loan /
              Investment. The disabled "Plain" placeholder (plain
              accounts only) keeps a nil role honest across saves. %>
          <select id="account_plan_role_<%= account.id %>" name="account[plan_role]"
                  class="text-sm border border-primary rounded-lg px-2 py-1.5 bg-container text-primary w-full">
            <%= options_for_select(role_options, account.plan_role.presence || "") %>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 pt-1 border-t border-subdued">
      <%# Remove from plan (owner round 3, R3): the form is the SIBLING
          below the main form (nested <form> is invalid HTML and the
          parser would swallow it). Assigned allocations persist
          unassigned with the "No Assignment" marker (never deleted).
          The in-place submit handler confirm()s when allocations
          are attached (data-remove-confirm + data-allocated-count). %>
      <button type="submit"
              form="bank_remove_<%= account.id %>"
              class="text-sm text-destructive hover:underline">
        <%= t(".remove") %>
      </button>
      <button type="submit"
              class="text-sm bg-primary text-on-primary rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 hover:opacity-90">
        <%= t(".save") %>
      </button>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <%# The remove-from-plan sibling form (nested <form> is invalid HTML):
      it must stay INSIDE the dialog — the in-place handler re-renders
      this whole dialog from the response on every save, and the sibling
      must come back fresh (its allocated_count is stale after a save). %>
  <%= form_with url: flow_account_remove_plan_path(account.id),
                method: :delete,
                id: "bank_remove_#{account.id}",
                class: "sr-only",
                data: {
                  turbo: "false",
                  plan_flow_inplace: "true",
                  remove_confirm: "true",
                  allocated_count: Current.family.plan_allocations.where(account_id: account.id).count,
                  remove_message: t(".remove_confirm", count: Current.family.plan_allocations.where(account_id: account.id).count)
                } do %>
  <% end %>
  <%# Round 25 (Item 2): the REVERSE sibling form (only when the account is
      dressed): the kebab item submits it (type=submit + form=). The
      in-place handler DELETEs the target allocation row; the response
      re-renders this whole dialog with the forward action back (the
      sibling, like bank_remove, must stay INSIDE the dialog so it comes
      back fresh on every save). %>
  <% if target_allocation %>
    <%= form_with url: flow_allocation_destroy_plan_path(target_allocation.id),
                  method: :delete,
                  id: "allocated_reverse_#{account.id}",
                  class: "sr-only",
                  data: { turbo: "false", plan_flow_inplace: "true" } do %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
<% end %>
